So this is my personal hot take.

28
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:19,080
我倾向于说 上下文工程有大约 80% 都是智能体搜索 因为就是这个
I like to say that context engineering is about 80% agentic search because it's this

29
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,040
这里的这个小方框
little box right here.

30
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:24,220
好 那我们先从一点小小的历史开始
All right. Let's start with a little bit of history.

31
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:25,580
当我说历史时
And when I say history,

32
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,860
指的其实就是过去三年
I mean the last three years.

33
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:32,460
说到 RAG（检索增强生成） 当我们一开始使用 RAG 时
RAG. When we started with RAG,

34
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:36,680
最初的想法是使用一条固定的检索流水线
the original idea was that we had a fixed retrieval pipeline.

35
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:46,400
所以用户的消息通常会几乎原封不动地被当作搜索查询
So the user message would usually more or less verbatim be used as a search query to be

36
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:52,620
通常作为向量搜索查询 从数据库中拉取一些数据或数据块
used usually as a vector search query to pull some data or chunks from a database.

37
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:55,620
然后连同检索到的上下文一起
And together with a retrieved context,

38
00:02:55,800 --> 00:03:00,840
用户消息会被放入上下文窗口 再一起送入大语言模型
the user message would go into the context window and then it would be fed to the LLM.

39
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:02,420
听起来还不错
Nice.

40
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:06,360
但这显然有很多局限
This has clearly many limitations.

41
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,060
因为这是一个固定的流水线
So since this is a fixed pipeline,

42
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,720
不管你实际上需不需要额外上下文
whether or not you actually need any context,

43
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:14,700
你都会去检索额外的信息
you're still retrieving additional information.

44
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,120
而在最糟糕的情况下
And in the worst case,

45
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:18,340
这些信息反而会把你的大语言模型搞糊涂 对吧
that can actually confuse your LLM, right?

46
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,520
另一方面 如果你只检索一次
On the other hand, if you're only retrieving once,

47
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:26,520
比如你需要做一些多跳检索
let's say you need some multi hop retrieval,

48
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:29,320
你在问大语言模型一个更复杂的问题
you're asking your LLM something more complex,

49
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:32,200
那么如果你只检索一次
then if you're only retrieving once,

50
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:37,700
也许第一次检索到的数据块里 暗示了你还需要发起另一个搜索查询
maybe the retrieved chunks reveal some information about another search query you need,

51
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:42,960
那你其实就会希望能进行第二轮搜索 对吧
then you would actually might want to have a second round of search, right?

52
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:46,800
这就是为什么后来我们转向了智能体 RAG
So that's why we then moved on to agentic RAG.

53
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:52,260
我们用一个搜索工具来替代原来的固定流水线
So we replaced the fixed pipeline with now a search tool.

54
00:03:52,960 --> 00:04:03,460
现在智能体可以自己决定要不要调用搜索工具 去检索一些信息
So now the agent can decide by itself whether or not to call the search tool and retrieve some information.

55
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:07,660
这样我们就不再有 “我到底需不需要额外信息” 这个问题
So we don't have the problem anymore of do I actually need any information?

56
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:10,300
而且当我真的去检索信息时
And when I actually retrieve information,

57
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,200
也可以判断这些信息是否相关
is this even relevant?

58
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:13,860
我是否需要再多检索一些
Do I need to retrieve more?

59
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:19,060
我是不是得先检索点什么
Do I actually have to retrieve something,

60
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:21,020
再重写搜索查询
rewrite the search query?

61
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:23,320
没错
Yeah.

62
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:30,540
不过在这种情况下 我们仍然只有一个上下文来源 也就是一个数据库
So we still only have one context source in this case, one database.

63
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:33,160
但当我们看上下文工程时
Now when we look at context engineering,

64
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:37,480
上下文分布在很多不同的地方 对吧
the context lies in many different places, right?

65
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:40,380
比如我们在本地文件里有上下文来源
So we have context sources in local files.

66
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:43,120
比如说你的编程智能体
So when you think about your coding agent,

67
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:50,760
你的代码项目或代码文件很可能就放在本地文件系统里
you probably have your coding project or code files laying around in your local file system.

68
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:54,680
也许你还在用某种工作记忆
Maybe you're using some kind of working memory,

69
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:59,680
比如一个草稿板 你会和智能体一起在上面规划你要做什么
like a scratch pad, so you're planning with your agent what you want to do,

70
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:02,580
那你大概会有一个类似 plan.md 的文件
then you probably have something like a plan.md file.

71
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,260
当你有智能体技能时
When you have agent skills,

72
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:08,940
它们通常也会放在某个本地文件夹里
you also have them usually in a local folder somewhere.

73
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,120
我们依然有数据库
We still have databases,

74
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:14,860
因为很多企业会把数据存放在数据库中
because many enterprises have their data stored in databases.

75
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:19,180
我们还有网络 作为另一个上下文来源
We have the web as another context source.

76
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:24,140
我知道这张图在这里会非常有争议
And I know this is a super controversial image here,

77
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:29,540
因为我没有明确把长期记忆放在本地文件系统里 还是放在数据库里
because I did not commit to having the long-term memory in the local file system or the database.

78
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:32,200
我觉得这目前是一个很大的讨论话题
This is, I think, currently a very big discussion.

79
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:35,020
如果你们愿意 我们可以在问答环节聊聊这个
We can get into this in the Q&A, if you like.

80
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:39,820
但无论如何 我们还有长期记忆 作为另一个上下文来源 对吧
But we also have long-term memory as another context source, right?

81
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:44,700
那我们究竟要如何从这些地方检索上下文呢
So how do we actually retrieve context from these?

82
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:47,420
通常我们会有一组
Usually we have a set of,

83
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:51,540
可以说是 “上下文来源原生” 的搜索工具
let's say, context source native search tools.

84
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,120
比如对于本地文件
So for the local files,

85
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:58,500
你通常会有类似搜索文件工具这样的东西
you usually have something like a search files tool.

86
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:01,900
对于技能 你通常会有一个技能加载工具
For skills, you usually have a skill loading tool.

87
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:04,360
当你想到数据库时
When you think about databases,

88
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:07,580
我们会有一些更定制化的工具
we have a little bit more custom tools.

89
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:12,280
比如一个语义搜索工具
So something like a semantic search tool.

90
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:16,220
也许你还会有一些更通用的工具
Maybe you also have something more general purpose,

91
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:20,760
比如一个可以对数据库执行完整搜索查询的工具
like a tool that lets you execute entire search queries against the database,

92
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:21,960
比如说 SQL 之类的
like SQL, for example.

93
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,920
对于网络 你会有网络搜索工具
For web, you have web search tools.

94
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:28,520
对于记忆 你会有类似专门的记忆工具
And for memory, you have something like a dedicated memory tool.

95
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,940
如果光是这些还不够让人觉得信息量爆炸
If that's not overwhelming enough,

96
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:35,060
我们现在还有一种叫做 Shell 工具的东西
we now also have something called a shell tool.

97
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:38,980
在 LangChain 里 它被称为 Shell 工具
Langchain calls it a shell tool.

98
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:41,440
在 Anthropic 里 它被称为 Bash 工具
Anthropic calls it the bash tool.

99
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:45,300
如果你用过 Claude Code
If you've played around with Claude Code,

100
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:46,700
它在那里被叫作 执行工具
it's called the exec tool.

101
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:51,760
但所有这些工具的共同点是它们都能让你的智能体在终端里运行命令
But what all of these tools do is they let your agent run commands in the terminal.

102
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:55,760
而这实际上让它们变得非常多才多用
And that actually makes them super versatile.

103
00:06:56,060 --> 00:07:04,700
因为现在你可以让智能体使用命令行工具来浏览和探索你的本地文件
Because now you can let your agent use CLIs to navigate and explore your local files.

104
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:09,560
这样你就可以直接运行 ls 和 grep 在本地文件系统中查找数据
So you can just run ls and grep to find data in your local file system.

105
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:15,320
如果你的数据库有自定义的命令行工具
If your database has a custom CLI,

106
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:21,600
你实际上可以让智能体也使用这个 Shell 工具来与数据库交互
you can actually let the agent also use the shell tool and interact with the database.

107
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:28,460
你还可以让智能体从零开始写出一整个脚本
You could also let your agent write an entire script from scratch,

108
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,940
比如连接到你的数据库
like connect to your database,

109
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,060
然后运行一个搜索查询
run a search query.

110
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:35,800
如果你的数据库通过 HTTPS 暴露出来
If your database is exposed via HTTPS,

111
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:37,780
你就可以直接运行一个 curl 命令
you can just run a curl command,

112
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,260
通过这个 Shell 工具与数据库交互
interact with the database through the shell tool.

113
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:46,080
说到 curl 命令，如果你愿意的话，你也可以进行网页搜索
Speaking of curl commands, you can also do web searches, if you like.

114
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:50,100
所以这个 Shell 工具是非常多才多用的，对吧
So this shell tool is super versatile, right?

115
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:57,820
所以今天的问题和主题是……我们到底需要什么样的搜索工具
So the question and the topic of today is... What search tool do we actually need?

116
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:00,340
我们只需要一个 Shell 工具吗
Do we only need a shell tool?

117
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:02,140
我需要所有这些工具吗
Do I need all of these?

118
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:07,240
如果你今天只能带走一个结论
And if you take home only one thing from today,

119
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:11,380
那就是要把搜索做好是非常困难的
it's that doing good search is incredibly difficult.

120
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:15,920
这也就是为什么我们有这么多不同的搜索技术，对吧
And that's why we have many different techniques to do search, right?

121
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:17,140
我们有向量搜索
We have vector search,

122
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,380
我们有关键词搜索
we have keyword search,

123
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:20,240
甚至在向量搜索里面
even in vector search,

124
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,980
我们有稠密嵌入
we have dense embeddings,

125
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:24,500
稀疏嵌入、多向量嵌入
sparse embeddings, multivector embeddings.

126
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:27,240
然后我们还有许多不同的索引技术
Then we have many different indexing techniques.

127
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:34,480
所以根据你在搜索需求和延迟需求上的不同
So depending on what kind of search requirements and latency requirements you have,

128
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:39,800
你就需要打造一套适合自己的搜索工具栈，对吧
you will need to curate your own stack of search tools, right?

129
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:44,180
所以今天我们会看其中的几种
So today we're going to be looking at a few of these.

130
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:45,980
很遗憾我们只有一个小时
Unfortunately we only have one hour,

131
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:47,940
所以我没法把所有的都展示给你们
so I cannot show you all of them.

